{:edb/db-before-t 12061 :edb/db-after-t 12062 :edb/tx-data [[13194139545374 50 #inst "2026-11-02T05:50:58.853Z" 13194139545374 17592186576411 true] [17592186233915 1071 "Given that $x=4\\sqrt{y}+3{y}^{5},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n<div class=\"question-equation fraction-equation\">\n<span>$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$</span>\n<span class=\"answer-fraction\">\n<span class=\"answer-fraction-numerator\">{{field-1}}</span>\n<span class=\"answer-fraction-denominator\">$2\\sqrt{y}\\,+${{field-2}}</span>\n</span>\n</div>" 13194139545374 17592186576411 true] [17592186233915 1071 "Given that $x=4\\sqrt{y}+3{y}^{5},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | $2\\sqrt{y}\\,+${{field-2}} |" 13194139545374 17592186576411 false] [17592186315109 1071 "Given that $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n<div class=\"question-equation fraction-equation\">\n<span>$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$</span>\n<span class=\"answer-fraction\">\n<span class=\"answer-fraction-numerator\">${y}^{3}$</span>\n<span class=\"answer-fraction-denominator\">{{field-1}}</span>\n</span>\n</div>" 13194139545374 17592186576411 true] [17592186315109 1071 "Given that $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | ${y}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" 13194139545374 17592186576411 false] [17592186315109 1074 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-1}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(-2{y}^{-3})+5(2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+10y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+10{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+10{y}^{4}}.\n$$" 13194139545374 17592186576411 false] [17592186315109 1074 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-2}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(-2{y}^{-3})+5(2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+10y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+10{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+10{y}^{4}}.\n$$" 13194139545374 17592186576411 true]] :edb/tempids {} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
